   "intro": "In 1967 the Beatles withdrew in the recording studio. Because of this the years 1967 and 1968 have become known as their studio years. The output was as psychedelic in content as impressive from a musical perspective. In February 1967 the group released the single Penny Lane / Strawberry Fields Forever ; followed in June by the album Sgt. Pepper's Lonely Hearts Club Band . Next in July the public got the surprise of the single All You Need Is Love / Baby You're A Rich Man . Then in November the single Hello Goodbye / I'm The Walrus was released, which already in December was followed by the double EP Magical Mystery Tour . March 1968 saw the single Lady Madonna / The Inner Light and the last days of August Hey Jude / Revolution . In July the cartoon movie Yellow Submarine made its way into the theaters (the songs were released on album in January 1969). The lack of albums that year was filled up in November with the White Album ."
  },
